The code logs 5 five times because `var` has function scope, not block scope. By the time each `setTimeout` callback runs, the loop has already finished and `i` has the final value 5. All callbacks share the same `i` variable.

To fix it, use `let` instead of `var`. `let` has block scope, creating a new binding of `i` for each iteration:

